stem_md:
Find the relation of the black part length and the white part length for the main diagonal of the 

a)  $100\times 99$  chess-board; 

b)  $101\times 99$  chess-board.

candidates:
\begin{align*}
    \lfloor \frac{10^n}{m}\rfloor = 1989 &\implies 1989 < \frac{10^n}{m} < 1990 
    &\implies \frac{10^n}{1990}<m<\frac{10^n}{1989} 
    &\implies 10^n \left(\frac{1}{1989}-\frac{1}{1990} \right) >1 
    &\implies n=7 \text{ is the minimum}
\end{align*}

