Let  $x_1\le\ldots\le x_n$  be the blue points and let  $y_1\le\ldots\le y_n$  be the red points. Then the question is equivalent to the inequality  $$ \sum_{j>i}\left(x_j-x_i\right)+\sum_{j>i}\left(y_j-y_i\right)\le\sum_{i,j}\lvert x_i-y_j\rvert. $$  It is true since
\begin{align*}
\sum_{j>i}\left(x_j-x_i\right)+\sum_{j>i}\left(y_j-y_i\right)&=\sum_{j>i}(x_j+y_j-x_i-y_i)
&\le\sum_{j>i}\left(\lvert x_j-y_i\rvert+\lvert y_j-x_i\rvert\right)
&\le\sum_{i,j}\lvert x_j-y_i\rvert.
\end{align*}

