<blockquote>
Let  $ABC$  be a triangle. Denote the midpoint  $U$  of the side  $[BC]$  and for the points  $P\in (AB) , N\in (AC)$  denote  $S\in PN\cap BC$  and the midpoint  $V$  of the segment  $[PN] .$  Prove that for a point  $M\in (BC)$  exists the equivalence  $\frac {MB}{MC}=\frac {SN}{SP}\ \Longleftrightarrow\ UV\parallel AM .$ </blockquote>
*Solution to Problem 539.*
Let  $A$  be the origin, let  $B$  and  $C$  have affixes  $b,c$  and let  $P,N$  have affixes  $\lambda  b, \mu c$  respectively.
