Now, after proving your claim, we may leave only the graph induced by  $S_1,S_2,S_3$  , then add additional vertex  $v$  and connect it with all vertices  $v_1,v_2,v_3$  were connected with. Let it would be the graph  $G'$ . 

Clearly any vertex in  $G'$  has degree at least  $3$  and  $G'$  has less edges then  $G$ . By minimality of  $G$  (or the induction hypothesis, depending on the approach) there is a cycle inside  $G'$  of length not multiple of  $3$ . Obviously that cycle is inside some  $S_i,i=1,2,3$  , hence it is also a cycle inside  $G$ .

