Now let  $Q$  be the intersection point of the  $A$ -angle bisector with  $O_bO_c$ ; observe that  $O_bO_c$  is the perpendicular bisector of  $\overline{AP}$ , and hence  $AQ = QP$ .  Now, since  $A,Q,M$  and  $N,O,M$  are collinear triplets of points,
\[
\angle QAP \equiv\angle MAP = \angle MNP \equiv\angle ONP,
\]
so triangles  $QAP$  and  $ONP$  are similar as well.  Thus  $\mathcal S$  also sends  $N$  to  $O$ .

But  $N$  is the midpoint of  $\overline{I_bI_c}$ , so  $O$  is the midpoint of  $\overline{O_bO_c}$ .  Done.

